---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import stories from '../../utils/short_stories.json'
import './styles.scss'

const anim = {
	old: {
		name: "bezier",
		duration: "0.4s",
		easing: "cubic-bezier(0.65,0.05,0.36,1)",
		direction: "reverse"
	},
	new: {
		name: "bezier",
		duration: "0.4s",
		easing: "cubic-bezier(0.65,0.05,0.36,1)"
	}
}

const customTransition = {
	forwards: anim,
	backwards: anim
}
---

<html lang="en" style="--bg-color: var(--bg-green)">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon/favicon-96x96.png" sizes="96x96" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="shortcut icon" href="/favicon/favicon.ico" />
		<link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/favicon/apple-touch-icon.png" />
		<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="〈物語〉" />
		<link rel="manifest" href="/favicon/site.webmanifest" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>Monogatari Series - Short Stories</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Here you'll find information about the Monogatari Series light novels, the anime adaptation and more!" />
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:title" content="〈物語〉Monogatari Series - Short Stories" />
		<meta property="og:description" content="Here you'll find information about the Monogatari Series light novels, the anime adaptation and more!" />
		<meta property="og:url" content="https://monogatariseri.es/" />
		<meta property="og:image" content="https://monogatari-series.vercel.app/banners/lns-banner.jpg" />
		<meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
		<meta property="twitter:url" content="https://monogatariseri.es/" />
		<meta property="twitter:title" content="〈物語〉Monogatari Series - Short Stories" />
		<meta property="twitter:description" content="Here you'll find information about the Monogatari Series light novels, the anime adaptation and more!" />
		<meta property="twitter:image" content="https://monogatari-series.vercel.app/banners/lns-banner.jpg" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Layout>
			<main>
				<div class="subsection">
					<h2>Short Stories</h2>
					<p>The Monogatari Series numerous "short stories" written primarily to complement the main narrative and provide extra context for specific events.</p>
					<p>While two official compilation books have been released, many other short stories were published individually and never made it into these volumes. A prime example is the collection of short stories included in the special editions of the Bakemonogatari manga.</p>
					<p>Thankfully, fans have created a compilation book also called Mijikanamonogatari, which collects <em>almost</em> every short story ever released. This volume includes the content of both official books, the manga short stories, and various individual releases.</p>
					<br />
					<p>Aside from those short stories, there are two additional crossover books. The first, titled called Tsukimonogatari (written as 月物語, meaning "Month Story"), features a crossover between Sangatsu no Lion's protagonist Kiriyama Rei and Hanekawa Tsubasa. It was released as a collaboration between Umino Chika (Sangatsu no Lion's author) and NisiOisiN.</p>
				 	<p>The second book is Mazemonogatari (written as 混物語, meaning "Mixed Story"), a spin-off crossover compilation that features Araragi Koyomi interacting with the characters from NisiOisiN's other works.</p>
					<p>If you want to read all of these stories, please refer to the <a href="/downloads/stories">short story downloads page</a>.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="titles">
					{stories.map(({ name, kanji, pictures }) => (
						<div class="book">
							<a class="cover" href={`/stories/${name}`}>
								<picture transition:name={`story-cover-${name}`} transition:animate={customTransition}>
									{pictures.map((path, i) => {
										const isLast = pictures.length === i + 1
										const type = path.split('.').pop()

										if (isLast) return <img src={path} alt="" loading="lazy" />
										
										return <source srcset={path} type={`image/${type}`} />
									})}
								</picture>
							</a>
							<div class="name">
								<ruby set:html={(kanji.filter(([kanji]) => !kanji.includes('(')).reduce((prev, [kanji, romaji]) => [...prev, `${kanji}${romaji ? `<rt>${romaji}</rt>` : ''}`], []).join(''))}>
								</ruby>
								{kanji.some(([kanji]) => kanji.includes('(')) &&
									<ruby class="small">
										{kanji.filter(([kanji]) => kanji.includes('('))[0][0]}<rt>{kanji.filter(([kanji]) => kanji.includes('('))[0][1]}</rt>
									</ruby>
								}
							</div>
						</div>
					))}
				</div>
			</main>
		</Layout>
	</body>
</html>
